        "text": "Security update for squid",
        "title": "Title of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "This update for squid fixes the following issues:\n\n- CVE-2025-62168: failure to redact HTTP authentication credentials in error handling leads to the disclosure of credentials a trusted client uses to authenticate (bsc#1252281).\n- CVE-2025-59362: SNMP message processing component of Squid Cache can lead to stack-based buffer overflow (bsc#1250627).\n",
